-- title:
--   Diamond automorphisms preserve Gauss p-integrality at level M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup assumed to contain every unit $u$ whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial. Fix $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ and two Laurent series $x, y \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ lying in the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$. Assume that $x$ and $y$ correspond under the diamond automorphism [`ModularCurve.diamondAutHBar M H d`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L32): pushing $x$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ by the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), viewing it as an element of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the image of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), and applying that automorphism yields the series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}(y)$. Here `diamondAutHBar M H d` is, by construction, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of that subfield satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d` whenever one exists — namely one which, for all weights $k$, all weight-$k$ forms $f, g$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose upper-left entry reduces to $d$ modulo $M$, sends the image of the ratio of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ to the image of an element of `xHFunctionField M H` whose complex $q$-expansion times that of $g \mid_k \gamma$ equals that of $f \mid_k \gamma$ — and is the identity otherwise. Finally, assume $x$ is Gauss $p$-integral: there are power series $a, a'$ with coefficients in the subring $\{q \in \mathbb{Q} : \gcd(\mathrm{den}(q), p) = 1\} = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ such that the reduction of $a'$ modulo $p$ (coefficientwise, via [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAtResidue`](def/GaloisRep_RatLocalizedAtResidue.html#L15)) is nonzero and $x \cdot a' = a$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. The conclusion is that $y$ is Gauss $p$-integral in the same sense: there exist $b, b'$ in $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[[q]]$ with $b' \not\equiv 0 \bmod p$ and $y \cdot b' = b$.
--
--   The assertion is that the diamond operator $\langle d\rangle$ preserves the valuation ring of the Gauss extension of the $p$-adic valuation to the function field of $X_H(M)$ — equivalently, the local ring at the generic point of the component through the cusp $\infty$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ — in the case where $p$ exactly divides $M$ and $H$ contains the kernel of reduction to level $M/p$. It feeds the non-vanishing statement [`ModularCurve.intSeriesC_ne_zero_of_coe_eq_slash_of_mem_Gamma0_of_level_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.intSeriesC_ne_zero_of_coe_eq_slash_of_mem_Gamma0_of_level_mul), which controls $q$-expansions of forms translated by matrices in $\Gamma_0(M)$.
